-- S23 Maharashtra prose — karla-bhaja-caves (REVERSE PATTERN: monsoon-best)
-- Verdict matrix: 10 go / 0 skip / 2 wait
-- Anchors: Karla Chaitya Hall (Cave 8) = TALLEST CHAITYA HALL IN INDIA at 14m, 124ft long;
--          37 octagonal pillars topped with elephant + couple sculptures, 2nd c BCE Hinayana;
--          Bhaja = 22 caves, 2nd c BCE, music-room cave 12 with rhythmic dance reliefs (unique);
--          Ekvira Devi temple at Karla = Mahar/Devadasi pilgrim site; Karla annual jatra Feb-Mar;
--          Lonavala 11km off NH48 Mumbai-Pune Expressway; ASI Rs 25 entry;
--          Pune 50km / Mumbai 90km; Buddha Purnima Tue May 26 2026.
-- *** REVERSE PATTERN: Jul-Aug peak monsoon = score 5; waterfalls on basalt cliffs the entire reason these caves are recommended ***

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('karla-bhaja-caves', 1, 'go', 4, 'The Karla-Bhaja cave cluster sits off the Mumbai-Pune Expressway near Lonavala — Pune 50km away (1h), Mumbai 90km (1.5h). Karla''s Cave 8 is the Chaitya Hall, the tallest of its kind in India at 14m (45ft) high and 124ft long, with 37 octagonal pillars topped by elephant-and-couple sculptural capitals — all 2nd century BCE Hinayana craft. Bhaja 12km away is a quieter 22-cave cluster with its famous music-cave-12 featuring rhythmic dance-relief panels found nowhere else in early Buddhist art. January gives the cluster dry-weather clarity — daytime 20-28C, low humidity, clean Sahyadri air. The Ekvira Devi temple at Karla draws Mahar and Devadasi pilgrim flow year-round but jatra peak is Feb-Mar. January is a quiet, photogenic month for serious cave study; chikki vendors fill Lonavala''s old market.', 'Dry Sahyadri winter with clean low-angle light on the 14m Karla Chaitya Hall pillars and Bhaja music-cave-12 dance reliefs; Lonavala chikki season and quiet pre-jatra temple courtyard.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 2, 'go', 5, 'February at Karla aligns with the start of the annual Ekvira Devi jatra — the temple at Karla''s base draws Mahar and Devadasi pilgrim flow from across Maharashtra during the Feb-Mar window. The temple sits within the Hinayana cave complex, creating a unique hybrid pilgrim-and-archaeological site where Buddhist 2nd-c-BCE chaitya hall and active Hindu Devadasi devotional practice share the same hill. Weather holds 22-30C with the cleanest light of the year. Maghi Buddha-context observances pull a small monastic flow but the main draw remains the Karla chaitya hall — its 37 octagonal pillars and the central stupa are at their photographic best in February''s low haze. Weekend Lonavala traffic spikes from Pune-Mumbai escape day-trippers; Sun mornings before 9am stay calm.', 'Ekvira Devi jatra opens at Karla in Feb-Mar drawing significant Mahar-Devadasi pilgrim flow; the temple-cave hybrid site shows active devotional practice alongside the 2nd-c-BCE Karla chaitya hall.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 3, 'go', 4, 'March continues the Ekvira Devi jatra window through the first half of the month before Holi (Mar 3 2026) and weather warming end the peak pilgrim flow. Daytime climbs 28-34C, mornings still 20-22C. Karla pilgrim numbers stay elevated Mar 1-15, then drop sharply Mar 16-31 as the heat builds. Gudi Padwa Mar 19 2026 pulls Marathi New Year regional traffic into Lonavala for chikki shopping but the caves themselves stay calm post-Ekvira. The 14m Karla chaitya hall interior at 23-25C feels noticeably cooler than the Lonavala parking lot outside, making midday viable for the cave itself even as the climb up to it gets warm. Bhaja''s 22 caves, accessed via a separate hill 12km from Karla, stay quiet — Bhaja is the introvert''s alternative if Karla feels crowded.', 'Last 2 weeks of Ekvira jatra Mar 1-15 plus the post-jatra calm Mar 16-31 give two distinct moods; Lonavala chikki shopping peaks with Gudi Padwa Mar 19 weekend traffic.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April brings pre-monsoon heat to the Lonavala plateau — 30-36C daytime, mornings 22-25C, humidity rising to 60-70%. The Karla cave hill climb (a 350-step ascent from the parking lot to the chaitya entrance) gets sweaty after 10am. Cave interiors hold cool at 24-26C from basalt thermal mass. April is the worst single month for Karla-Bhaja visitor density-to-weather ratio — Pune-Mumbai schools break mid-month and weekend families flood Lonavala for chikki, lake walks, and cave visits. The Bhaja side stays quieter than Karla. Serious photographers wait for monsoon; serious heritage visitors come at 5:30am, finish by 9am, and retreat to Lonavala chikki shops. Buddha Purnima is in May, not April. No specific April Buddhist anchor.', 'Pre-7am cave-hill climb in cool air with cave interiors at 24-26C still rewarding for serious heritage visitors; weekday off-peak hours give nearly-empty Bhaja cluster.', 'After 10am the 30-36C heat plus weekend Lonavala chikki tourism crowds make the 350-step Karla climb and queue-bottlenecked chaitya entrance fatiguing.'),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 5, 'wait', 3, 'May is peak heat at Lonavala — 33-37C daytime, humidity climbing to 70-75% as monsoon approaches. The 350-step Karla climb is genuinely difficult after 9am. Buddha Purnima falls Tue May 26 2026, the most important Theravada and Mahayana lunar anniversary. Karla''s chaitya hall sees Theravada monastic chants and Maharashtrian Navayana Buddhist offerings on May 26 — the 14m hall, lit by ceremonial lamps, holds 100+ pilgrims comfortably. The Ekvira Devi temple inside the cave complex also runs Buddha Purnima observances alongside its regular Hindu devotional flow. Outside May 26, the month is best spent at lower-altitude cooler destinations. Lonavala''s tourist traffic stays high (school holidays continue) so post-cave chikki shopping is busy. Heat-fatigue is real on multi-cave day combining Karla + Bhaja.', 'Buddha Purnima Tue May 26 2026 lights up the 14m Karla chaitya hall with monastic chants, ceremonial lamps, and a 100+ pilgrim assembly — the single most atmospheric day for Karla all year.', 'Outside the May 26 Buddha Purnima window, 33-37C heat with 70-75% humidity makes the 350-step Karla climb difficult after 9am; the Karla + Bhaja combined day-trip accumulates dangerous heat-fatigue.'),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 6, 'go', 4, 'June flips the Karla-Bhaja calendar. The southwest monsoon arrives in Lonavala typically Jun 7-14 — the western Sahyadri ridge catches the first heavy rainfall on the subcontinent. Within days of monsoon onset, basalt cliffs on both Karla and Bhaja hills begin shedding waterfalls; the entire hillside becomes the visual experience the caves were carved against. Bhaja''s south-facing cliff line in particular develops a cluster of cascades that fall directly past the cave 12 music-room. Karla''s chaitya hall stays dry inside, but the approach climb is now in rain. Mumbai-Pune Expressway sections see Khandala-Lonavala mist warnings. The Ekvira Devi temple courtyard floods in heavy spells. This is when Karla-Bhaja becomes a Sahyadri monsoon destination, not a heritage day-trip — pack rain gear and accept the chaos.', 'Southwest monsoon arrives Jun 7-14 turning the Karla and Bhaja basalt cliffs into waterfall faces; Bhaja cave-12 music-room sits directly under one of the seasonal cascades — the visual rationale these caves were carved for begins to reveal itself.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 7, 'go', 5, 'July is Karla-Bhaja''s annual peak month. The western Sahyadri ridge receives some of the highest July rainfall in India outside the Konkan and Cherrapunji belts. Karla''s entire basalt cliff face becomes a waterfall — the chaitya hall entrance overlooks a 50m+ seasonal cascade. Bhaja''s south-facing cliff line develops 4-5 distinct waterfalls. The cave 12 music-room with its 2nd-c-BCE dance reliefs sits beneath one cascade; cave 18 with its stupa cluster catches another. Photography is dramatic and the spiritual logic — why Hinayana monks chose these cliffs over Karla''s 37 octagonal pillared chaitya entrance — becomes architecturally obvious. The Mumbai-Pune Expressway has Khandala-Lonavala fog and aquaplaning advisories; the Karla cave-hill steps are slippery but climbable. This is the single reason these caves are recommended in Maharashtra travel writing.', 'Peak monsoon turns Karla and Bhaja into the Western Ghats'' most dramatic Buddhist-cave-cum-waterfall site; the 50m cascade at Karla chaitya entrance and Bhaja cave-12 waterfall reveal exactly why Hinayana monks chose this cliff line in 2nd c BCE.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 8, 'go', 5, 'August continues the peak monsoon spectacle. Lonavala-Khandala receives some of its highest August rainfall on record (the Pune district averages 800-1000mm in August alone). Karla and Bhaja waterfalls are at full flow. The greater Lonavala-Khandala scenic belt — Tiger Point, Bushi Dam, Pavna Lake, Tikona Fort — is all at peak too. The Karla chaitya hall interior stays dry through the heaviest rain; basalt overhangs work. The challenge is the 350-step climb to Karla''s entrance in rain — wear grip-soled shoes and budget for slow ascent. The Ekvira Devi temple stays operational. Bhaja, with its 22 caves spread across a single hillside accessed via 200 steps, is easier wet-weather logistics than Karla. The Bhaja waterfalls past cave 12 are at photographic peak. Sankashti Chaturthi Aug 4 brings small Ganesh-anchor flow.', 'Continued peak monsoon spectacle with Karla and Bhaja waterfalls at full force; the cluster of greater Lonavala-Khandala monsoon sights (Tiger Point, Bushi Dam, Pavna Lake) makes a full Sahyadri monsoon day-trip from Pune the textbook itinerary.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 9, 'go', 4, 'September is the monsoon tail. Rain tapers from Sep 15 onward; Karla and Bhaja waterfalls reduce in flow week by week, with the largest cascades drying up by month-end. The hillsides stay full green through October. Sahyadri air is washed clean. Daytime 24-28C in early month, climbing to 26-30C by month-end. Ganesh Chaturthi falls Sep 12 2026 — Lonavala temples and the Ekvira Devi shrine at Karla run Ganeshotsav observances Sep 12-22, drawing Maharashtrian devotional weekend traffic. The cave complex itself stays calm of pilgrims but Lonavala chikki shops are busy through the festival window. The 350-step Karla climb is back to dry-grip safety from Sep 20 onward. Mid-month is the inflection — committing too early gets you tail-end rain, too late misses the waterfall finale.', 'Monsoon tail with Karla-Bhaja waterfalls reducing but the green hillsides at annual peak; Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12-22 lights up Lonavala-side Ekvira temple courtyard alongside the cave-archaeological site.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is the post-monsoon clarity peak. Sahyadri air is glass-clear; daytime 24-30C, low humidity 55-65%, mornings cool at 18-20C. The Karla and Bhaja hillsides stay deep green from monsoon refill. Waterfalls reduce to trickles but the basalt cliff geometry the caves were carved into is at its most legible. Karla chaitya hall morning light from 7:30am to 10am rakes across the 37 octagonal pillars showing carving detail unavailable in any other month. Bhaja''s cave 12 music-room dance reliefs photograph cleanly. Weekend Lonavala day-tripper traffic rises sharply from Oct 15; weekday mornings stay calm. Sharad Purnima Oct 25 2026 pulls some Marathi devotional traffic to Ekvira temple but the caves themselves stay quiet on weekdays. Combined Karla + Bhaja day-trip from Pune or Mumbai works comfortably.', 'Post-monsoon clarity peaks with glass-clear Sahyadri air, deep-green hillsides, ideal morning light on Karla''s 37 octagonal pillars, and cool dry conditions for the combined Karla + Bhaja day-trip itinerary.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is Karla-Bhaja''s most comfortable dry-weather month. Daytime 22-28C, nights 14-18C, humidity 50-60%, zero rain, glass-clear visibility. The 350-step Karla climb is easy in cool dry air. Lonavala''s broader scenic belt (Tiger Point lookout, Lion''s Point, Bhushi Dam) is at year-round visual peak with clear long-distance Sahyadri views. Karla cave 8 chaitya hall and the central stupa photograph at their architectural sharpest. Bhaja cave 12 dance reliefs are at peak study conditions. No specific November Buddhist anchor but weekend Pune-Mumbai escape tourism is at year-round peak through the entire Lonavala belt — book lodging Fri-Sun nights at least 14 days ahead. Weekday mornings stay calm enough for unhurried 4-hour cave-study sessions. Kartik Purnima Nov 24 brings small devotional flow to Ekvira temple courtyard.', 'Cool, dry, and visually clearest dry-weather month with year-round-peak Sahyadri visibility for the wider Lonavala belt; ideal for unhurried 4-hour cave-study sessions across both Karla and Bhaja.', NULL),
('karla-bhaja-caves', 12, 'go', 4, 'December continues Karla-Bhaja''s dry-weather best — daytime 20-27C, nights 12-16C, no rain, low humidity. The Lonavala-Khandala belt is at its annual tourist peak as Pune-Mumbai families fold the area into year-end leave and school holidays. Weekend Karla parking lot fills by 9am; the 350-step climb to the chaitya entrance has continuous foot-traffic Sat-Sun. Weekday mornings 7am-10am stay calm. Margashirsha Purnima Dec 24 is a minor Marathi devotional anchor. Christmas-New Year week (Dec 25-Jan 2) sees year-round-peak Lonavala tourism; mid-month (Dec 5-15) is closer to November-calm. Cool air makes Bhaja''s 200-step climb genuinely pleasant. Lonavala chikki season peak — Maganlal Chikki (since 1924) and the broader chikki-makers'' market lane near the railway station is at year-round busiest.', 'Continued dry-clear December gives easy step-climbs at both Karla and Bhaja in cool air; year-round-peak Lonavala chikki season combined with school-holiday family tourism but mid-month stays workable for serious heritage visitors.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
